{"name":"Ghost Ship","hex":"#887b6e","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"ghost ship","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An abandoned ship, or  spaceship, that is haunted and possibly adrift.","Synonym of shadow ship."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ghost_ship"}],"entries":[{"title":"The Ghost Ship","blocks":[{"text":"The Ghost Ship is a 1943 American black-and-white psychological thriller film starring Richard Dix and directed by Mark Robson. It was produced by Val Lewton for RKO Radio Pictures as part of a series of low-budget horror films. The film can be seen as a \"low-key psychological thriller\", a \"suspense drama\", and a \"waterlogged melodrama\". Russell Wade, Edith Barrett, Ben Bard and Edmund Glover appear in support."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/44/The_Ghost_Ship_%281943_poster%29.jpg/330px-The_Ghost_Ship_%281943_poster%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Ghost_Ship","wikidata":"Q3228001"},{"title":"Ghost Ship (1952 film)","blocks":[{"text":"Ghost Ship is a 1952 British second feature horror film directed by Vernon Sewell and starring Dermot Walsh and Hazel Court. It was written by Sewell and Philip Thornton. This was one of four attempts by Sewell to adapt and film the Pierre Mills and Celia de Vilyars Grand Guignol stage play L'Angoisse."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/8/82/%22Ghost_Ship%22_%281952_film%29.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ghost_Ship_(1952_film)","wikidata":"Q5557149"},{"title":"Ghost Ship (2002 film)","blocks":[{"text":"Ghost Ship is a 2002 supernatural horror film directed by Steve Beck from a screenplay by Mark Hanlon and John Pogue. Its plot follows a marine salvage crew in the Bering Sea who discover a mysterious ocean liner that disappeared in 1962 and stars an ensemble cast of Gabriel Byrne, Julianna Margulies, Ron Eldard, Desmond Harrington, Isaiah Washington, Alex Dimitriades, and Karl Urban."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/5/55/Ghost_Ship_poster.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ghost_Ship_(2002_film)","wikidata":"Q1356265"},{"title":"Ghost ship","blocks":[{"text":"A ghost ship, also known as a phantom ship, is a vessel with no living crew aboard; it may be a fictional ghostly vessel, such as the Flying Dutchman, or a physical derelict found adrift with its crew missing or dead, like the Mary Celeste. The term is sometimes used for ships that have been decommissioned but not yet scrapped, as well as drifting boats that have been found after breaking loose of their ropes and being carried away by the wind or the waves."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f2/Deering2.jpg/330px-Deering2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ghost_ship","wikidata":"Q281019"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/18/Flying_Dutchman%2C_the.jpg/500px-Flying_Dutchman%2C_the.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/18/Flying_Dutchman%2C_the.jpg/500px-Flying_Dutchman%2C_the.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The Flying Dutchman by Albert Pinkham Ryder","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AFlying_Dutchman%2C_the.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c1/Epave_Marlborough.JPG/500px-Epave_Marlborough.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c1/Epave_Marlborough.JPG/500px-Epave_Marlborough.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_c